cuems-audioplayer (0.0.3-12) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * End-of-file limit in output-channel bytes (1amfwm7e4wv). The stream
    always has 2 ports, so a mono file is reopened as stereo; the limit was
    still computed for 1 channel, so at the JACK rate (no resampling) it was
    half the real length and the first MTC re-sync past the middle
    silenced the cue until its end. Reproduced by itself on a Behringer
    UMC204HD box (clock -242 ppm vs MTC: a re-sync every ~5.5 min) at 10:44
    into a 15:06 mono file, the lleida-diposit failure. The conversion log
    now says Upmixing/Downmixing correctly.
  * "Out of file boundaries!" is logged once per entry into the past-end
    state, with the seek position and the limit in ms, instead of on every
    audio callback (1amfwm7e4x3, ~25 000 lines per failed pass).
  * Zero-fill after a short read compares bytes with bytes: the end of
    every file no longer replays 2-5 ms of the previous period (D3).
  * Rig evidence: cuems-RELATIONS baselines/1amfwm7e1pq-mono-eof.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:37:30 +0200

cuems-audioplayer (0.0.3-11) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Never let RtAudio auto-connect the outports to system:playback_*
    (869fcvz85, 869fcvzag): the stream is opened with
    RTAUDIO_JACK_DONT_CONNECT. The engine always wires a player to the mixer,
    and an auto-connect that landed after that wiring stayed, so the cue
    sounded through the mixer and straight to the outputs, doubled and
    outside the mixer's volume and mute. A player started by hand, outside
    the engine, is silent until it is connected with jack_connect.
  * Build-Depends: librtaudio-dev (>= 5.1), the first RtAudio with the flag
    (5.2.0 in bookworm), so a build against an older library fails loudly
    instead of silently dropping it.
  * UNRELEASED until the live check on node01 (cuems-RELATIONS
    Plans/2026-10-06-engine-audio-arm-port-wait.md).

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

cuems-audioplayer (0.0.3-10) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Hold silence on a negative seek instead of terminating the cue
    (869dyufeh). audioCallback's MTC-correction boundary check conflated
    two cases in one else branch: a future-anchored cue, whose start_mtc
    is still ahead of live MTC and therefore yields a negative
    seekPosition, took the same path as a genuine past-end read and set
    outOfFile=true. That skipped the read block, so count stayed 0 and
    the cue died with 'Out of file boundaries!' before it ever played.
    Split three ways: seekPosition < 0 holds silence and keeps waiting;
    0..fileSize seeks and plays; > fileSize is a real end of stream. The
    player becomes self-gating — it can follow MTC early and start
    itself at start_mtc — which is the prerequisite for the engine
    dropping its per-cue reveal OSC. Until now this fix existed only as
    an unpushed local branch, so no deb and no host in the fleet carried
    it, and the engine's deferred /mtcfollow was the only thing keeping
    future-anchored audio cues alive.

 -- Ion Reguera <ion@stagelab.coop>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 14:07:47 +0200

